# Summary
Introduced non-security bug: the new diagnostic guidance links are unreachable because their hosts were not added to the existing trustedExternalURL allow-list.
The new diagnostic report guidance adds two inline buttons that call openURL with hard-coded URLs on www.google.com and keys.openpgp.org. The Wails bridge routes this through App.OpenURL, which validates the target using trustedExternalURL. That function only allows github.com, hatolife.booth.pm, support.discord.com, and x.com. As a result, clicking the newly added gpg-file search link or public-key link returns an error and does not open the browser. This is a UI/functionality regression, not a security vulnerability, because the allow-list remains restrictive and does not expose arbitrary URL opening.

